.TH "shellkin\-feature" "5" "March 2026" "shellkin\-feature(5)" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]shellkin\-feature\f[R] \- feature file for shellkin
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shellkin feature files use a small Gherkin\-compatible subset for
describing test scenarios.
.PP
Feature files are loaded from the selected features directory and must
use the \f[B].feature\f[R] extension.
.SH SUPPORTED KEYWORDS
Shellkin currently supports these Gherkin keywords:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Feature\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Background\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Rule\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Scenario\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Scenario Outline\f[R], \f[B]Examples\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Given\f[R], \f[B]When\f[R], \f[B]Then\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]And\f[R], \f[B]But\f[R], \f[B]*\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
data tables
.SH FORMAT
.SS Feature Header
Each feature file starts with a \f[B]Feature:\f[R] header.
.IP
.EX
Feature: \-\-help
.EE
.SS Description Text
Free text may appear below the feature header before the first section.
.IP
.EX
Feature: \-\-help
  Show help message
.EE
.SS Scenario
Each executable example is declared with \f[B]Scenario:\f[R].
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Run \-\-help
  When I run \(aqshellkin \-\-help\(aq
  Then the output should include \(aqshellkin COMMAND\(aq
.EE
.SS Background
Use \f[B]Background:\f[R] for steps that should run before each scenario
in the feature.
.IP
.EX
Background:
  Given I am in a temp directory
.EE
.SS Rule
Use \f[B]Rule:\f[R] to group scenarios that illustrate one business
rule.
Tags on a Rule are inherited by every scenario in that Rule.
Free\-form description text may appear below the Rule header.
.IP
.EX
\(atadmin
Rule: Administrators can manage users
  Administrators have access to user management.

  Scenario: Deactivate a user
    When I deactivate user \(aqAlice\(aq
    Then user \(aqAlice\(aq should be inactive
.EE
.PP
A Rule may have one \f[B]Background:\f[R] before its first scenario.
Feature Background steps run first, followed by Rule Background steps.
.IP
.EX
Background:
  Given the current user is \(aqDana\(aq

Rule: Administrators can manage users
  Background:
    Given the current role is \(aqadmin\(aq

  Scenario: Deactivate a user
    When I deactivate user \(aqAlice\(aq
    Then user \(aqAlice\(aq should be inactive
.EE
.SS Scenario Outline
Use \f[B]Scenario Outline:\f[R] with one \f[B]Examples:\f[R] table to
run the same scenario with several values.
Each Examples row is a separate scenario.
.IP
.EX
Scenario Outline: Creating <name> as <role>
  When I register user \(aq<name>\(aq with role \(aq<role>\(aq
  Then user \(aq<name>\(aq should have role \(aq<role>\(aq

Examples:
  | name  | role   |
  | Alice | admin  |
  | Bob   | member |
.EE
.PP
Placeholders may appear in the scenario name, steps, doc strings, and
data table cells.
Every placeholder must have a matching Examples column.
Examples headings must be unique, and all rows must have the same number
of cells.
.PP
Shellkin currently supports one Examples block per Scenario Outline.
Tags on Examples blocks are not supported.
.SS Steps
Supported step keywords are \f[B]Given\f[R], \f[B]When\f[R],
\f[B]Then\f[R], \f[B]And\f[R], \f[B]But\f[R], and \f[B]*\f[R].
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Touch a file
  Given I am in a temp directory
  When I run \(aqtouch somefile\(aq
  Then the file \(aqsomefile\(aq should exist
.EE
.PP
\f[B]And\f[R], \f[B]But\f[R], and \f[B]*\f[R] reuse the semantic type of
the previous step.
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Run command
  When I run \(aqshellkin \-\-help\(aq
  And the exit code should mean success
.EE
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Prepare files
  Given I am in a temp directory
  When I run \(aqtouch one\(aq
  * I run \(aqtouch two\(aq
  Then the file \(aqone\(aq should exist
  And the file \(aqtwo\(aq should exist
.EE
.PP
Like \f[B]And\f[R] and \f[B]But\f[R], the \f[B]*\f[R] keyword cannot be
the first step in a scenario or background.
.SH COMMENTS AND BLANK LINES
Blank lines are ignored.
.PP
Lines starting with \f[B]#\f[R] are treated as comments.
.IP
.EX
# This is a comment
Feature: Example
.EE
.SH TAGS
Tags can be placed before a \f[B]Feature:\f[R] or \f[B]Scenario:\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\(atfilesystem
Feature: Files

\(atsmoke
Scenario: Create a file
  When I run \(aqtouch one\(aq
  Then the file \(aqone\(aq should exist
.EE
.PP
Feature tags are inherited by the scenarios in that feature.
Use \f[B]shellkin \-\-tag \(attag\f[R] to run scenarios with a tag, and
\f[B]shellkin \-\-exclude\-tag \(attag\f[R] to skip scenarios with a
tag.
.SH DOC STRINGS
Shellkin supports Gherkin\-style doc strings using
\f[B]\(dq\(dq\(dq\f[R] fences.
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Match multiline output
  When I run \(aqprintf \(dqhello\(rsnworld\(dq\(aq
  Then the output should match
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
    hello
    world
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
.EE
.PP
The doc string content is exposed to the matching step definition
through the \f[B]DOC_STRING\f[R] environment variable.
.SH DATA TABLES
A data table may follow a step.
Its first row is exposed to the matching step definition as the
\f[B]TABLE_HEADER\f[R] array.
Each remaining row is stored as a tab\-separated value in the
\f[B]TABLE_ROWS\f[R] array.
.IP
.EX
Given these users exist
  | name  | role  |
  | Alice | admin |
  | Bob   | user  |
.EE
.PP
All rows must contain the same number of cells.
Cell values are trimmed.
Escaped pipe characters in cells are not currently supported.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.EX
Feature: file creation
  Basic file operations

Background:
  Given I am in a temp directory

Scenario: Create a file
  When I run \(aqtouch somefile\(aq
  Then the file \(aqsomefile\(aq should exist
.EE
